# Git commit messages

Write commit messages as a single line only. No body, no footer, no HEREDOC extra paragraphs.

Prefer conventional commits with a scope when useful:

```text
feat(home): add non-sticky navbar
fix(writing): skip empty GitHub links
chore: add Astro/npm gitignore
docs(product): lock MVP clarifications
```

Do not write multi-line messages like:

```text
chore: add Astro/npm gitignore

Keep dependencies, build output, and env files out of version control.
```
